# Git must NEVER touch line endings in this project.
#
# Every file the MSX reads is CR+LF and has to stay that way byte for
# byte - see CLAUDE.md, "File rule: anything the MSX reads is CR+LF". A
# source file silently converted to LF assembles as one enormous line and
# reports "Unterminated macro constuction", which says nothing about line
# endings. That has cost an evening once already.
#
# "-text" means: no conversion, in either direction, ever. Store and check
# out exactly the bytes that are here.

* -text
